    "content": "# SUJET OFFICIEL BAC SM 2018 - ANGLAIS\n**Session Officielle 2018 | MEPU-A Guinée**\n\n---\n\nMEPU-A/SNESCO\n\n                                 BACCALAUREAT - SESSION 2018\n\n                                 Profils : Sciences Mathématiques / Sciences Expérimentales \n\n                                 Epreuve de : Anglais \n\n                                 Coefficient : 2 \n\n                                 Durée : 2 heures \n\n                                 Sujet \n\n\t Chose the appropriate words fill in the blanks (5pts)\n\n\t  Nationalities, defeated, people, invalided, escaped, mercenaries, organized, battle, fought, back, trial.  \n\n\tJust around 2 am at night on November 22, 1970 &hellip;&hellip;.. of various attacked Guinea. They &hellip;&hellip;. Conakry, koundara and other strategy places such as the tombo power center, the radio station, camp boiro etc. immediately after, the &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;. That are civilians and soldiers &hellip;&hellip;&hellip; themselves and &hellip;&hellip;.. the enemy. Others were &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip; either during &hellip;&hellip;. Or after their &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;.\n\n\t Write a tag question for each of the following statements. (2,5pts)\n\n\tYou are 26 years old, &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;..?\n\n\tAmadou plays handball, &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;.?\n\n\tYour family doesn’t live in Kindia, &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;?\n\n\tAminata and Djodjo are not ugly, &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;..?\n\n\tThey have got 500GF, &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;..?\n\n\t Use comparative or superlative form with the adjectives in parentheses to complete the following sentences. (2,5pts)\n\n\tAlima is &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;. Than Mariame (  nice  ).\n\n\tDJodjo is the &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip; student of the classroom. (  lazy  )\n\n\tA plane is &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip; than a car. (  comfortable  )\n\n\tSidiki is &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;.. Than his brother. (  kind  )\n\n\tJacknis is the &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;. Of the family (  shy  )\n\n\t Transform these active sentences into passive sentences. (3pts)\n\n\tMamady and Ousmane will buy a car.\n\n\tI play football every Sunday.\n\n\tThe students did an evaluation yesterday.\n\n\t In one paragraph write about what you will do if you get your baccalaureate, at least 15 lines. (7pts) \r\n\n                                    NB : Cette version est une version transcrite des extraits de l’originale. Elle peut\n                                    donc contenir des erreurs de frappe,\n                                    d’orthographe ou de données."
